":"criterion","findings":["RC-01"],"decisions":[],"why":"RC-01 removed `not(native_correlated delivered)` from this criterion because it contradicted the only edge that could reach the phase. A conjunct removed for a stated reason is one removal away from the next one having no reason at all, so what REMAINS is pinned: the failure is owned, not merely declared.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/remaining_duties","/payload/receipts","/payload/service_window"],"why":"the obligations survive on the record, and the receipts actually obtained and the window are recorded -- a failure that recorded none of these would be a closure wearing the word failure"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/performer_assignment","states_exactly":["accepted"],"optional":false}],"why":"CAP-30: failure creates a support/remedy duty, and a duty with no accepted performer is unowned"}]},{"predicate_id":"criterion.GrievanceCase.remedy_authorized.v1","kind":"criterion","findings":["G4-02"],"decisions":[],"why":"G4-02: `remedy_reservation_refs` was required in the payload and used by 0 predicates, and this criterion carried `nonempty_fields: []` -- so a remedy could be authorized with no reservation at all, which is what made CAP-42's funded remedy prose.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/remedy_reservation_refs"],"why":"an empty reservation list is the exact shape the finding names"},{"op":"related_phases","bindings":[{"field_path":"/payload/remedy_reservation_refs","states_exactly":["held","partly_consumed"],"optional":false}],"why":"the funding is ACTUALLY RESERVED: every entry resolves to a live Reservation. A released or expired reservation funds nothing."}]},{"predicate_id":"criterion.GrievanceCase.triaged.v1","kind":"criterion","findings":["G4-01"],"decisions":[],"why":"G4-01: `disputed_custodian` is required on GrievanceCase and was read by 0 of 2,255 predicates. The criterion carries the two ref