"AD-017"],"why":"R-D13 and R-X27, pinned where the boundary is crossed: a model-to-model return exists only on a declared procedure edge, delivers TYPED OUTPUTS only, and stores prose at a Ref UNDELIVERED. The typed-member rule extends to every transfer the fixtures name, including the work-order dispatch and the founder-facing brief.","require":[{"op":"nonempty_fields","field_paths_include":["/payload/constraint_set_ref","/payload/return_payload_kind"],"why":"the typed constraint set and the kind of the return are both named on the crossing"},{"op":"eq","contains_pointers":["/payload/return_payload_kind"],"right":"typed_outputs","why":"the return delivers typed outputs. This is section 9's adverse row 15: a return delivering prose"},{"op":"eq","contains_pointers":["/payload/prose_delivery"],"right":"ref_only","why":"and prose is stored at a Ref rather than delivered -- evidence, never a substitute for a member the receiver can restate as a typed value"}]},{"predicate_id":"edge.Fulfillment.delivering.delivered.v1","kind":"guard","findings":["G2-05"],"decisions":["AD-013"],"why":"G2-05/AD-013 at the guard layer: an authenticated attributable delivery event AND native correlation. Each is one line nothing would notice the removal of.","require":[{"op":"transition_basis","event_kind":"record.delivered","why":"delivery needs an authenticated attributable delivery event, and it must be THAT event kind"},{"op":"native_correlated","result":"delivered","why":"... natively correlated against the delivery adapter, never against the payment"}]},{"predicate_id":"edge.Fulfillment.delivering.failed.v1","kind":"guard","findings":["RC-01"],"decisions":[],"why":"The in-flight failure route RC-01 added, and the layer that CAN say what the criterion could not: this edge, unlike the one from `delivered`, asserts that no observation correlates a delivery.","require":[{"op":"transition_basis","event_kind":"record.delivery_failed","why":"an authenticated attributable failure event; withou