the guard is unreachable rather than detached, and the phase on the far side of it is unreachable with it. Measured at bcfd658: three such deletions on these records, three runs, three exit 0."},{"record":"StepExecution","from":"running","to":"reported","findings":["F6D-04","F6D-01"],"why":"This edge is where `guard.effect.one_per_step` is attached. Deleting the TRANSITION is a different attack from deleting the call: the edge predicate survives, the attachment pin still resolves, and the route simply no longer exists -- so the guard is unreachable rather than detached, and the phase on the far side of it is unreachable with it. Measured at bcfd658: three such deletions on these records, three runs, three exit 0."},{"record":"StandingHolder","from":"suspended","to":"staffed","findings":["F6D-04"],"why":"And the way back. Without it a suspension is permanent, so suspending a holder closes the duty class rather than pausing it, and the guard above becomes a one-way ratchet nobody would use."},{"record":"InstrumentCalibration","from":"scheduled","to":"run","findings":["F6D-04"],"why":"The only route into `run`, which is the phase 06 section 7 requires a checker's calibration to stand in before its verdict may satisfy an acceptance gate. Deleted, no calibration can ever reach `run` and every verdict is from an uncalibrated instrument -- the rule holds vacuously, which is the worst way for it to hold."},{"record":"EffectIdentity","from":"claimed","to":"observed","findings":["F6D-04"],"why":"The reconciliation route. Deleted, an effect identity can be claimed and never observed, so the detection of an already-released effect before a business action repeats -- 05 section 6's stop rule -- has no terminal state to reach."},{"record":"WorkflowDefinition","from":"draft","to":"admitted","findings":["F6D-06"],"why":"This edge is where `guard.grant.declared_resolves_to_live_grant` is attached. Deleting the TRANSITION is a different attack from deleting the call: the edge predica